WHEREAS the Board is desirous of engaging a competent contractor for the implementation of community health outreach services in selected Local Government Areas of Kano State for a period of twenty-four (24) months;

WHEREAS the Contractor has represented and warranted that it possesses the requisite expertise, personnel, and resources to execute the services aforesaid;

WHEREAS the parties have agreed to enter into this Contract on the terms and conditions hereinafter contained;

NOW THEREFORE, IT IS HEREBY AGREED AS FOLLOWS:

ARTICLE 1: DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION

1.1 In this Contract, unless the context otherwise requires:
(a) "Board" means the Kano State Primary Health Care Board;
(b) "Contract Price" means the total sum payable to the Contractor for the full and proper performance of the Services;
(c) "Effective Date" means the date of execution of this Contract by both Parties;
(d) "Services" means the community health outreach implementation services described in Article 2 and the Statement of Works attached hereto as Schedule A;
(e) "Site" means the communities and health facilities within the designated Local Government Areas as specified in Schedule B;
(f) "State" means Kano State of Nigeria.

ARTICLE 2: SCOPE OF SERVICES

2.1 The Contractor shall provide the following services:
(a) Planning, coordination, and execution of community health outreach sessions in rural and peri-urban communities across the designated Local Government Areas;
(b) Mobilisation of community members for routine immunisation, antenatal care, and health education;
(c) Deployment of mobile health teams comprising community health extension workers, nurses, and health educators;
(d) Provision of health education materials and community sensitisation programmes on maternal and child health, malaria prevention, and communicable disease control;
(e) Data collection and reporting on outreach activities to the Board's Monitoring and Evaluation Unit;
(f) Any other duties as may be reasonably directed by the Board's Programme Manager in writing.

2.2 The Services shall be performed in accordance with the detailed specifications contained in Schedule A and the work plan approved by the Board.

